    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d110">

                <pb facs="0168" n="76" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg76"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d110-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-09">9 November 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>No. 497. Prime Minister to President. Personal and most Secret, Your 411.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d110-f2"/></p>
                <pb facs="0169" n="77" xml:id="pg77"/>
                <p>Casey tells me that Kirk did not feel
                    entitled to telegraph to you till he heard from the State Department about
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >Sextant</hi>. He is proud and delighted to know that you will use his
                    house and all preparations are proceeding actively to that end.</p>
                <p>I leave by sea 12th reaching Gibraltar evening 15th, arriving Malta by air dawn
                    16th. I shall spend two or three days in the field with Alexander, meeting you at <hi rendition="#small-caps">Oboe</hi>, or if you
                    prefer, and I think it would be better fun, at Malta.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d110-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d110-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the United States Military Attaché, London, apparently via military
                    channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d110-f2" n="2" xml:id="d110-f2-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg71">p. 71</ref>.</p>
